usage: janus [-h] [--environment ENVIRONMENT] [--project-root PROJECT_ROOT]
             [--with-spark] [--source-id SOURCE_ID] [--run-id RUN_ID]
             [--started-at STARTED_AT] [--execute] [--ingest-raw-to-bronze]
             [--bronze-table BRONZE_TABLE] [--include-disabled] [--resume]

Validate JANUS runtime configuration, plan one source, or execute one
configured source through the framework runtime. Use `janus run-all [options]`
to execute enabled sources once in dependency order.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --environment ENVIRONMENT
                        Environment profile name under conf/environments
                        without the .yaml suffix.
  --project-root PROJECT_ROOT
                        Project root used to resolve conf/ and data/ paths.
  --with-spark          Create and stop a Spark session after validating the
                        environment config.
  --source-id SOURCE_ID
                        Configured source_id to plan from the source registry.
  --run-id RUN_ID       Optional explicit run identifier for the planned
                        source execution.
  --started-at STARTED_AT
                        Optional timezone-aware ISO-8601 timestamp used to
                        make planning deterministic.
  --execute             Execute the selected source through planning,
                        extraction, Spark normalization, bronze writes,
                        validation, and metadata persistence.
  --ingest-raw-to-bronze
                        Skip extraction, rediscover the selected source raw
                        artifacts already stored in the raw zone, and load
                        them into a bronze table informed at the CLI.
  --bronze-table BRONZE_TABLE
                        Target bronze table name for --ingest-raw-to-bronze.
                        Accepts either table_name or namespace.table_name.
  --include-disabled    Allow planning or executing a source that is
                        configured but disabled.
  --resume              Resume extraction from the last recorded page instead
                        of starting over. Reads the extraction_progress.json
                        written by a previous partial run and re-uses already-
                        fetched raw files. Has no effect if no progress file
                        exists.
